CWPP MUSIC PROMPT — chorus ignition archetype (late-60s psychedelic rock)

High-level intent (constraint framing):
Summon a late-1960s psychedelic rock anthem centered on ritualistic ignition, desire, and vocal incantation, optimized to lock onto a chant-like chorus hook with hypnotic repetition and escalating intensity, evoking the primal call-and-response energy associated with a Iconical Pyschedelic band from 1960's

Musical DNA (hard constraints)
Tempo: ~112–116 BPM, steady, trance-friendly
Meter: 4/4, minimal swing
Key center: A minor or D minor (modal, blues-psychedelic)
Harmony: Static vamp (i–♭VII–♭VI feel), minimal chord movement to sustain hypnosis
Groove: Locked, almost mechanical rhythm section — drummer rides hi-hat relentlessly, snare dry and forward, kick unwavering

Instrumenta
Organ: Vox Continental / Farfisa-style combo organ, slightly overdriven, pulsing eighth-notes, dominant in the mix
Guitar: Clean to lightly saturated electric guitar, tremolo + spring reverb, short stabbing chords during chorus
Bass: Repetitive, circular bassline, no fills, mantra-like
Drums: Tight kit, no flourish — the groove never breaks
Vocal FX: Subtle plate reverb + slapback delay, intimate but commanding
Vocal Character (critical CWPP lever)
Male vocal, baritone, sultry and hypnotic
Delivery feels spoken-sung, intimate, slightly dangerous
Chorus vocals escalate from invitation → command → near-chant
Breath and phrasing are audible; phrasing stretches around the beat
Chorus Construction (the summoning engine)
Short, repetitive imperative phrase
Built to be sung by a crowd, not just the lead
Melody spans a narrow range — emphasis on rhythm and tone, not pitch jumps
Each repetition grows louder, closer, more insistent

